  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "The University of South Carolina is a public research university in Columbia, South Carolina, founded on 19 December 1801 as South Carolina College. It is classified as an R1 Doctoral University with the highest research activity and enrols over 38,000 students at its Columbia campus, with more than 52,000 across the wider USC system. The historic Horseshoe at the heart of campus preserves 11 buildings from 1805–1850s under towering oaks.",
      "USC is organised into 16 colleges and schools, including the McCausland College of Arts and Sciences, Darla Moore School of Business, Molinaroli College of Engineering and Computing, Arnold School of Public Health, College of Nursing, Joseph F. Rice School of Law, School of Medicine Columbia and Greenville, and the South Carolina Honors College. The Darla Moore School of Business is consistently top-ranked nationally for its International Business programmes.",
      "Research strengths include energy, cybersecurity, aerospace, materials, public health, and nursing. USC houses the largest Robert Burns collection outside Scotland and the world's largest Ernest Hemingway collection. Athletics compete in the Southeastern Conference as the Gamecocks, with Colonial Life Arena and Carolina Stadium anchoring the campus.",
      "International students join from over 100 countries and benefit from 28 residence halls, Living Learning Communities, the South Carolina Honors College, and dedicated international student services. Columbia's location in the state capital provides internships in government, finance, and healthcare alongside year-round Southern climate."
    ],
    "paragraphsRu": [
      "University of South Carolina — государственный исследовательский университет в Columbia, штат Южная Каролина, основан 19 декабря 1801 года как South Carolina College. Классифицируется как R1 Doctoral University с высшим уровнем научной активности. На главном кампусе обучается более 38 000 студентов, в системе USC — свыше 52 000. В центре кампуса — исторический Horseshoe с 11 оригинальными зданиями 1805–1850-х под старыми дубами.",
      "USC состоит из 16 колледжей и школ, включая McCausland College of Arts and Sciences, Darla Moore School of Business, Molinaroli College of Engineering and Computing, Arnold School of Public Health, College of Nursing, Joseph F. Rice School of Law, School of Medicine Columbia and Greenville и South Carolina Honors College. Darla Moore School of Business стабильно входит в национальный топ по International Business.",
      "Сильные направления исследований: энергетика, кибербезопасность, аэрокосмос, материаловедение, public health, nursing. В библиотеке USC хранится крупнейшая коллекция Robert Burns за пределами Шотландии и крупнейшая в мире коллекция Ernest Hemingway. Спортивные команды Gamecocks выступают в Southeastern Conference; Colonial Life Arena и Carolina Stadium — ключевые арены кампуса.",
      "Международные студенты приезжают из более 100 стран и получают доступ к 28 резиденциям, Living Learning Communities, South Carolina Honors College и отдельным сервисам для international students. Расположение в столице штата открывает стажировки в правительстве, финансах и здравоохранении на фоне круглогодичного южного климата."
    ],
